    <node id="GraphRAG">
      <data key="d0">GraphRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A community-based traversal method for retrieval, which LightRAG reduces overhead compared to by focusing on retrieving entities and relationships instead of text chunks.&lt;SEP&gt;A graph-based retrieval-augmented generation system that uses graph-based text indexing for information retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;A graph-enhanced RAG system that extracts entities and relationships from text, represents them as nodes and edges, generates descriptions, aggregates nodes into communities, and produces community reports to capture global information.&lt;SEP&gt;A competitive baseline retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) method used for comparison with LightRAG&lt;SEP&gt;A graph-based retrieval method used as a baseline for comparison with LightRAG, leveraging graph-based text indexing for information retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;GraphRAG is a baseline model or framework for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) that relies on community structures and token-intensive processes for information retrieval and updates.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization or framework that uses community structure and regeneration to incorporate new entities and relationships, requiring substantial token costs for report reconstruction.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Movie Recommendation Systems">
      <data key="d0">Movie Recommendation Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Systems designed to predict user preferences for movies and provide personalized recommendations&lt;SEP&gt;Movie Recommendation Systems are systems designed to evaluate and optimize the accuracy and user satisfaction of movie recommendations using various metrics.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mean Squared Error">
      <data key="d0">Mean Squared Error</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Mean Squared Error (MSE) is a metric used to evaluate the accuracy of recommendation systems by measuring the average squared difference between predicted and actual values.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Root Mean Squared Error">
      <data key="d0">Root Mean Squared Error</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) is a metric used to evaluate the accuracy of recommendation systems by measuring the square root of the average squared differences between predicted and actual values.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Area Under the Curve">
      <data key="d0">Area Under the Curve</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Area Under the Curve (AUC) is a metric used to evaluate the performance of recommendation systems by measuring the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="F-Measure">
      <data key="d0">F-Measure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric combining precision and recall to evaluate the balance between the two in recommendation systems, often used interchangeably with F1 Score&lt;SEP&gt;F-Measure is a metric used to evaluate the performance of recommendation systems by combining precision and recall into a single value.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User Engagement Metrics">
      <data key="d0">User Engagement Metrics</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">User Engagement Metrics are metrics used to evaluate the satisfaction and interaction levels of users with recommendation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Precision">
      <data key="d0">Precision</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric measuring the accuracy of positive predictions in recommendation systems&lt;SEP&gt;Precision is a metric used to evaluate the performance of recommendation systems by measuring the proportion of relevant recommendations among the total recommendations made.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recall">
      <data key="d0">Recall</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric measuring the ability of a recommendation system to identify all relevant items&lt;SEP&gt;Recall is a metric used to evaluate the performance of recommendation systems by measuring the proportion of relevant recommendations that are successfully retrieved.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mean Average Precision at K">
      <data key="d0">Mean Average Precision at K</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Mean Average Precision at K (MAP@K) is a metric used to evaluate the ranking quality of recommendation systems by measuring the average precision at various cutoff points.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Legal Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A subset of the UltraDomain benchmark covering legal topics, used in the evaluation of the LightRAG framework.&lt;SEP&gt;A dataset containing millions of tokens used to evaluate the performance of retrieval methods, particularly in legal contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal Dataset is a dataset used for evaluating the performance and cost efficiency of LightRAG and GraphRAG in terms of tokens and API calls.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Token">
      <data key="d0">Token</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Token is a unit of data used in computational processes, particularly in API calls and retrieval mechanisms for recommendation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="API Call">
      <data key="d0">API Call</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">API Call is a request made to an application programming interface to retrieve or process data, often used in retrieval-augmented generation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Community Report">
      <data key="d0">Community Report</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Community Report is a structured output generated by GraphRAG that summarizes entities and relationships within a community for retrieval purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Incremental Text Update">
      <data key="d0">Incremental Text Update</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Incremental Text Update is a process for integrating new data into existing recommendation systems or knowledge graphs without requiring complete regeneration.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C_max">
      <data key="d0">C_max</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">C_max denotes the maximum number of tokens allowed per API call in the retrieval process for GraphRAG, contributing to token overhead calculations.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C_extract">
      <data key="d0">C_extract</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">C_extract indicates the number of API calls required for entity and relationship extraction during the incremental text update phase for both LightRAG and GraphRAG.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval Phase">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval Phase</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval Phase is the initial stage in recommendation systems where relevant information is retrieved from a knowledge base or dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Answer 1">
      <data key="d0">Answer 1</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Answer 1 is a response evaluated for its comprehensiveness, diversity, and empowerment in assessing movie recommendation systems, focusing primarily on traditional metrics.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Answer 2">
      <data key="d0">Answer 2</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Answer 2 is a response evaluated for its comprehensiveness, diversity, and empowerment in assessing movie recommendation systems, providing a broader array of metrics and nuanced explanations.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval Mechanism refers to the process or system used by LightRAG to integrate graph structures and vectorized representations for efficient information retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Level-2 Communities">
      <data key="d0">Level-2 Communities</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Level-2 Communities are a subset of communities generated by GraphRAG, specifically 610 in this experiment, used actively for retrieval purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Low-Level Retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Low-Level Retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A retrieval strategy focused on extracting precise information about specific nodes or edges&lt;SEP&gt;A retrieval approach focusing on precise information about specific entities and their relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;A detail-oriented retrieval process focused on extracting precise information about specific nodes or edges within a knowledge graph, including entities and their associated attributes or relationships.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="High-Level Retrieval">
      <data key="d0">High-Level Retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A retrieval strategy aggregating information across multiple entities and relationships for broader insights&lt;SEP&gt;A retrieval approach encompassing broader topics and themes to provide comprehensive responses.&lt;SEP&gt;A broader retrieval process that aggregates information across multiple related entities and relationships to provide insights into higher-level concepts and summaries rather than specific details.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Query Keyword Extraction">
      <data key="d0">Query Keyword Extraction</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process in LightRAG where local and global query keywords are extracted from a given query to facilitate keyword matching with entities and relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Keyword Matching">
      <data key="d0">Keyword Matching</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A retrieval step where local query keywords are matched with candidate entities and global query keywords with relations linked to global keys using a vector database.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Incorporating High-Order Relatedness">
      <data key="d0">Incorporating High-Order Relatedness</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process that enhances queries by gathering neighboring nodes within local subgraphs of retrieved graph elements to improve comprehensiveness of results.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval-Augmented Answer Generation">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Answer Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method where a general-purpose LLM generates answers based on retrieved information, including concatenated values from relevant entities, relations, and original text excerpts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Graph-Based Index Phase">
      <data key="d0">Graph-Based Index Phase</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A phase in the LightRAG framework where an LLM extracts entities and relationships from text chunks, requiring LLM calls proportional to the total tokens in the chunk size.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Graph-Based Retrieval Phase">
      <data key="d0">Graph-Based Retrieval Phase</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A phase in the LightRAG framework where relevant keywords are generated for each query, and vector-based search is used to retrieve entities and relationships, reducing retrieval overhead compared to GraphRAG.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UltraDomain Benchmark">
      <data key="d0">UltraDomain Benchmark</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation dataset sourced from 428 college textbooks across 18 distinct domains, including agriculture, social sciences, and humanities, used to assess the effectiveness of the LightRAG framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agriculture Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Agriculture Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A subset of the UltraDomain benchmark focusing on agricultural practices, covering topics such as beekeeping, hive management, crop production, and disease prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;A dataset containing millions of tokens used to evaluate the performance of retrieval methods, particularly in agricultural contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CS Dataset">
      <data key="d0">CS Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A subset of the UltraDomain benchmark focusing on computer science, encompassing key areas like data science, software engineering, machine learning, and big data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A dataset containing millions of tokens used to evaluate the performance of retrieval methods, particularly in computer science contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mix Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Mix Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A subset of the UltraDomain benchmark containing a mix of domains, used in the evaluation of the LightRAG framework.&lt;SEP&gt;A mixed dataset combining elements from Agriculture, CS, and Legal datasets, used to evaluate retrieval methods across diverse domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vector Database">
      <data key="d0">Vector Database</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A database system used in LightRAG to match local and global query keywords with candidate entities and relations through vector-based search.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-68c5b57fc5e4f80b4481763ee3f107c6-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1786372041</data>
